ascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317971\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325377\n", "files": ["dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream_impl.h"], "git_node": "11390942575a9f1d6977907e369b8914e787440d", "git_parents": ["cb44b558ee93e0c533aabfd312f7361f912a1680"], "node": "f03d3d4690bf707731fe486c7a32799dbcbcb112", "parents": ["3c76eef9dc644087ab9d3b099ae182f682ca7500"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054736 - Quota input stream parser: make sure buffer storing decrypted data is not left uninitialized.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322317\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325378\n", "files": ["dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream_impl.h"], "git_node": "0d4c76e3ae5cde9f370dd410b0f0e76e730c0d32", "git_parents": ["11390942575a9f1d6977907e369b8914e787440d"], "node": "5b4b950521dd30e947f1a9be71929c69cbf11ff0", "parents": ["f03d3d4690bf707731fe486c7a32799dbcbcb112"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054736 - Quota input stream parser: decrypt the previous block when seeking on EOF so mPlainBuffer contains the expected data.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322324\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325379\n", "files": ["dom/quota/DecryptingInputStream_impl.h"], "git_node": "3c64f479fef23e03ca63854cc17fa5a7039b6772", "git_parents": ["0d4c76e3ae5cde9f370dd410b0f0e76e730c0d32"], "node": "e38c79427508d32a1fc0fc90b55d5a8be93cc3a1", "parents": ["5b4b950521dd30e947f1a9be71929c69cbf11ff0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789408231, "git_changesets": ["11390942575a9f1d6977907e369b8914e787440d", "0d4c76e3ae5cde9f370dd410b0f0e76e730c0d32", "3c64f479fef23e03ca63854cc17fa5a7039b6772"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28485": {"changesets": [{"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071064 - Call ClearForm when unlinking form controls.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325435\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325510\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLImageElement.cpp", "dom/html/nsGenericHTMLElement.cpp"], "git_node": "ca31e0610a98c139bd41cfb7d3442de611f69c73", "git_parents": ["3c64f479fef23e03ca63854cc17fa5a7039b6772"], "node": "245898778daaf05c628f444892b8a7c39ef916d7", "parents": ["e38c79427508d32a1fc0fc90b55d5a8be93cc3a1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789410997, "git_changesets": ["ca31e0610a98c139bd41cfb7d3442de611f69c73"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28486": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071179 - Prevent image function from ending up as WR fallback.  a=pascalc\n\nThe image() function is incorrectly falling back to a blob image.\n\nUse an exclusive switch so that it doesn't happen again. The only thing\nwe don't support in the WR path as far as I can tell is -moz-element().\n\n-moz-symbolic-icon() works just like url(), and all the cases for url()\nwhere we return false there's basically nothing to draw. cross-fade() is\nnot implemented in either path so let's return true for now so that we\nintentionally switch to false if needed.\n\nI don't get the EffectiveAppearance() check and I don't think it's\nneeded. Those go through\nnsDisplayThemedBackground::CreateWebRenderCommands, and any\nauthor-specified background disables the native appearance.\n\nWhile at it don't bother to create WR commands for transparent colors,\nwhich are common in the front-end and is a one-liner check.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325399\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325686\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp", "layout/painting/nsImageRenderer.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-color-background-combined.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-color-background-position.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-color-background-repeat.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-color-background-size.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-color-basic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-color-layered.html.ini"], "git_node": "9c5dfd5e6bec64b5cc6a4687166cf487e082e81b", "git_parents": ["ca31e0610a98c139bd41cfb7d3442de611f69c73"], "node": "55d237d63ba6d942161e34fd1be5df572c322170", "parents": ["245898778daaf05c628f444892b8a7c39ef916d7"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789411045, "git_changesets": ["9c5dfd5e6bec64b5cc6a4687166cf487e082e81b"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28487": {"changesets": [{"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070481 - Don't apply the snap outset to an outset box-shadow's ClipOut  a=pascalc\n\nBug 2052033 passed the spread as the clip snap outset on both zero-blur\nbox-shadow arms. Only inset needs it, where the ClipOut is the element\ndeflated by the spread. An outset shadow's ClipOut is already the element,\nand anchoring it to snap(element.inflate(spread)) inset by the spread\ndiffers from snap(element) whenever spread * device_scale is fractional,\nso a border or background the element paints in the same colour no longer\nmeets the shadow and a partial-coverage seam flickers as the element moves.\n\nThe reftest fills the element in the shadow colour so the correct result is\nthe snapped shadow rect, solid. It uses spread 10.5 at scale 1, and no\nscale(*), because an integral spread * scale is the one case the bug cannot\nshow in.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324811\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325691\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/boxshadow/outset-abutting-fill-snap-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/boxshadow/outset-abutting-fill-snap.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/boxshadow/reftest.list"], "git_node": "d34bc6dca2410c86459cb0b54994230fb072af4d", "git_parents": ["9c5dfd5e6bec64b5cc6a4687166cf487e082e81b"], "node": "debbf675c9e8ce08ce8ca0d898f395500b7992f5", "parents": ["55d237d63ba6d942161e34fd1be5df572c322170"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789411111, "git_changesets": ["d34bc6dca2410c86459cb0b54994230fb072af4d"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28488": {"changesets": [{"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071499 [Linux] Don't crash when rendering to hidden X11 window  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325823\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325942\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "acbd4c1a4910a9f3de006ca276eee7ef919450c6", "git_parents": ["d34bc6dca2410c86459cb0b54994230fb072af4d"], "node": "bb823033bcac27801806aa51730fa0c2d4d9548c", "parents": ["debbf675c9e8ce08ce8ca0d898f395500b7992f5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789411501, "git_changesets": ["acbd4c1a4910a9f3de006ca276eee7ef919450c6"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28489": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071270 - Keep track of whether a general-enclosed query is a style query.  a=pascalc\n\nSo that we invalidate properly when it changes.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325722\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325933\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/queries/condition.rs", "servo/components/style/queries/feature.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-conditional/container-queries/style-range-var-in-function-change.html"], "git_node": "02dfa76bf03ee11ff72915ea2404c69234225f7c", "git_parents": ["acbd4c1a4910a9f3de006ca276eee7ef919450c6"], "node": "8708177c05e0abfbf942036c356932b9a378a415", "parents": ["bb823033bcac27801806aa51730fa0c2d4d9548c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789412456, "git_changesets": ["02dfa76bf03ee11ff72915ea2404c69234225f7c"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28490": {"changesets": [{"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070675 - Use the Adjust dynamic callbacks partner for Skyflag attributed users.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324748\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325927\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/AdjustMetricsService.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/AdjustMetricsServiceTest.kt"], "git_node": "48c9f5668552f317d458f43107b54ffa4cd33ff7", "git_parents": ["02dfa76bf03ee11ff72915ea2404c69234225f7c"], "node": "5e5d92884e8efa8b5afff3dfd1a738c2d82b4666", "parents": ["8708177c05e0abfbf942036c356932b9a378a415"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789412487, "git_changesets": ["48c9f5668552f317d458f43107b54ffa4cd33ff7"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28491": {"changesets": [{"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062965 - Tell Smart Window chat tabs apart by their conversation when closing duplicate tabs  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324446\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325912\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindowTabStatesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_duplicate_chat_tabs.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d770c43735cc5010a625b0edc1564c0f655807bd", "git_parents": ["48c9f5668552f317d458f43107b54ffa4cd33ff7"], "node": "c899ed9770fdd2503b051131a22007944feeeff4", "parents": ["5e5d92884e8efa8b5afff3dfd1a738c2d82b4666"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064054 - Make the Organize Tabs flyout a dismissable popup so Wayland can place it beside the panel  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324447\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325913\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button_interaction.js"], "git_node": "78c3420f7726ef28eacc9f5af04849c57aa33b11", "git_parents": ["d770c43735cc5010a625b0edc1564c0f655807bd"], "node": "bfa8249e5a3b19029ba990f3080d67599130075a", "parents": ["c899ed9770fdd2503b051131a22007944feeeff4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063568 - Keep Organize Tabs from suggesting a group name the user's groups already use  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324448\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325914\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGroupingSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button_suggestions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_AutoTabGrouping.js"], "git_node": "8567966ac0aebe60eeeb94a24188836ba21b73d4", "git_parents": ["78c3420f7726ef28eacc9f5af04849c57aa33b11"], "node": "282b8b3d2db32739ac3724efcc2ac492b90d3159", "parents": ["bfa8249e5a3b19029ba990f3080d67599130075a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2064041 - Let a slow Organize Tabs clustering run finish and fill the panel in instead of dropping its groups  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324449\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325915\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button_model.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button_suggestions.js"], "git_node": "898f3068bb307cdf6329f43a371c9ab1b876f048", "git_parents": ["8567966ac0aebe60eeeb94a24188836ba21b73d4"], "node": "32e7766d0c2a74a2ec6d380b5ed43e84a26f7be1", "parents": ["282b8b3d2db32739ac3724efcc2ac492b90d3159"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789412646, "git_changesets": ["d770c43735cc5010a625b0edc1564c0f655807bd", "78c3420f7726ef28eacc9f5af04849c57aa33b11", "8567966ac0aebe60eeeb94a24188836ba21b73d4", "898f3068bb307cdf6329f43a371c9ab1b876f048"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28492": {"changesets": [{"author": "Teodor Tanasoaia \u003cttanasoaia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1976766 - Stop assuming a buffer is still mapped in the GPU process.  a=pascalc\n\n`MapCallback`, `BufferUnmap`, `ReadbackPresentCallback` and\n`ReadbackSnapshotCallback` all read a buffer's mapped range while\nassuming it is still mapped. `MapCallback` is not invoked by wgpu-core\ndirectly but from a task, so content can destroy or unmap the buffer, or\nits device, before it runs. And once a device is lost or destroyed\nwgpu-core destroys all of its buffers in `release_gpu_resources`, at the\nend of whichever poll drains the device's queue; that poll is driven by\nthe GPU process, with no content involvement and no ordering against\ncontent's messages.\n\nReturn a null ptr for `DestroyedResource` and `NotMapped` rather\nthan panicking, and handle that at each call site: send a map error to\ncontent, skip the write-back flush, or skip the readback. `MapCallback`\nalso has to tolerate the parent's `mapData` for the buffer being gone,\nwhich can be caused by content destroying or dropping the buffer.\n\nRelated fixes:\n\n- moved `MapCallback`'s `get_mapped_range` call out of the read-only\n  branch so every map is checked.\n\n- `Buffer::Unmap` previously cancelled a pending map without telling the\n  GPU process, so content saw the buffer as unmapped while wgpu-core\n  still\n  had it mapped. Forwarding that unmap is what makes the `NotMapped`\n  race\n  above reachable.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324946\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325910\n", "files": ["dom/webgpu/Buffer.cpp", "dom/webgpu/ipc/WebGPUParent.cpp", "gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/server.rs", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/buffer/mapping/cts.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/buffer/mapping/dedicated.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/buffer/mapping/service.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/webgpu/cts/webgpu/api/validation/buffer/mapping/shared.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a55e6bc5b353c1fb9577a38f2dd6a1e8ee1f979", "git_parents": ["898f3068bb307cdf6329f43a371c9ab1b876f048"], "node": "70da4dec3bd4db4274adfd0934bfd0087bd2cc52", "parents": ["32e7766d0c2a74a2ec6d380b5ed43e84a26f7be1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789412739, "git_changesets": ["9a55e6bc5b353c1fb9577a38f2dd6a1e8ee1f979"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28493": {"changesets": [{"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 1: Request an input trust authority for a clear lead video stream.  a=pascalc\n\nBug 2022030 Part 5 (D287632) made `IsEncrypted()` return false on the clear\nlead segment to reflect the real encryption status. That function also tells\nMedia Foundation whether the stream needs the protected media path, which a\nclear lead still does because the encrypted part follows in the same stream.\n\nThe video descriptor was therefore marked `MF_SD_PROTECTED`, but the\n`IMFInputTrustAuthority` Media Foundation asked for while resolving the\ntopology was refused with `MF_E_NOT_PROTECTED`. It cannot resolve a protected\nbranch without one, so the topology failed with `MF_E_TOPO_UNSUPPORTED`.\nReverting this makes clear lead PlayReady streams play on Netflix again.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325208\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325888\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFMediaEngineVideoStream.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFMediaEngineVideoStream.h", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFMediaSource.cpp"], "git_node": "fd282966805f2de272d2c933c69eab9e4a036f18", "git_parents": ["9a55e6bc5b353c1fb9577a38f2dd6a1e8ee1f979"], "node": "acfeaf7cd7db52c1b13c574658068d1505778e70", "parents": ["70da4dec3bd4db4274adfd0934bfd0087bd2cc52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 2: Add a pref to disable the protected activation recovery, off by default.  a=pascalc\n\nWhen activation failed with `MF_E_TOPO_UNSUPPORTED` or\n`MF_E_INCOMPATIBLE_SAMPLE_PROTECTION` we re-drove the protected pipeline\nthrough the hardware-context-reset path, which closes every session with\nreason `hardware-context-reset`. Per the EME specification that invites the\napplication to create new sessions and retry, so a conformant player retries\nindefinitely. Netflix reported this as repeated `F7717-1273 (unexpected\nhardware-context-reset)`.\n\nNeither error is documented as transient. Microsoft publishes no guidance for\neither code, and Chromium, which drives the same Media Engine and PlayReady\npath, treats both as terminal and reserves hardware-context-reset for\n`DRM_E_TEE_INVALID_HWDRM_STATE` alone. The retry could not have helped in any\ncase, because `ExternalEngineStateMachine::SetCDMProxy` does not re-send the\nCDM proxy to the recreated engine, so the new engine never sets its media\nsource and never builds a topology.\n\nThe mechanism is left in place behind a pref so this can be flipped back on a\nrelease branch if disabling it regresses something. Removing it belongs in a\nfollow-up.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325209\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325889\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFProtectedPathReadinessMonitor.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/gtest/TestMFProtectedPathReadinessMonitor.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "935d8c98451ba8e51bc34be53f01b0a10b506237", "git_parents": ["fd282966805f2de272d2c933c69eab9e4a036f18"], "node": "a370c9e71324643e450dd68ec04581e2221978fa", "parents": ["acfeaf7cd7db52c1b13c574658068d1505778e70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 3: Log the image size and encryption state of the media engine setup.  a=pascalc\n\nThe metadata log reported only the display size, and the media source summary\nreported neither size, so both now carry the image and display size.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325210\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325890\n", "files": ["dom/media/ExternalEngineStateMachine.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/MFMediaEngineParent.cpp"], "git_node": "74da2ebc57cd77a858ecc25f8e436ac0241980ef", "git_parents": ["935d8c98451ba8e51bc34be53f01b0a10b506237"], "node": "e15b9fac314a5eecffd00814944819ecd1d57c36", "parents": ["a370c9e71324643e450dd68ec04581e2221978fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071106 - Part 4: Test that a clear lead stream is granted an input trust authority.  a=pascalc\n\nAdds TestMFMediaSourceProtection, which builds an MFMediaSource the way\nMFMediaEngineParent does and drives IMFTrustedInput against a mock CDM.\n\nThe failure this covers needs SL3000 hardware DRM and a licence server, so it\ncannot be reached from a mochitest, but we can test it on gtest.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325211\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325891\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/gtest/TestMFMediaSourceProtection.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "d6dd6150c79c377a5d25c0fd3260449edf39774b", "git_parents": ["74da2ebc57cd77a858ecc25f8e436ac0241980ef"], "node": "ad1a84d2008e7ba9c463f1eea31cad40164d14be", "parents": ["e15b9fac314a5eecffd00814944819ecd1d57c36"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789412864, "git_changesets": ["fd282966805f2de272d2c933c69eab9e4a036f18", "935d8c98451ba8e51bc34be53f01b0a10b506237", "74da2ebc57cd77a858ecc25f8e436ac0241980ef", "d6dd6150c79c377a5d25c0fd3260449edf39774b"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28494": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063658 - [devtools] Only set cors disabling headers for network overrides.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324090\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325859\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkObserver.sys.mjs", "devtools/shared/network-observer/NetworkOverride.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e4c07597deeb004aad5bfae52c3ae641455cc242", "git_parents": ["d6dd6150c79c377a5d25c0fd3260449edf39774b"], "node": "e5bb9e38912cfbb31aa6950bc434e2d250d59d3b", "parents": ["ad1a84d2008e7ba9c463f1eea31cad40164d14be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063658 - [devtools] Assert that local mode requests are blocked by CORS.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324091\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325860\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/network-observer/test/browser/browser_networkobserver_localMode.js"], "git_node": "618e70e0f63bfb29c23fd08d5e0bc3fbd21d980f", "git_parents": ["e4c07597deeb004aad5bfae52c3ae641455cc242"], "node": "1ec3e91e8f68f23e9a2a552426ca8da597e0ca8c", "parents": ["e5bb9e38912cfbb31aa6950bc434e2d250d59d3b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789413210, "git_changesets": ["e4c07597deeb004aad5bfae52c3ae641455cc242", "618e70e0f63bfb29c23fd08d5e0bc3fbd21d980f"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28495": {"changesets": [{"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070562 - about:addons default and AMO curated nova themes preview should follow the current OS light/dark mode.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324746\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325851\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons-utils.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/theme-preview.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_themes_picker.js"], "git_node": "8870e22c00ca9facfa41bea479f4090d840837ad", "git_parents": ["618e70e0f63bfb29c23fd08d5e0bc3fbd21d980f"], "node": "b5a060dfc4a2cb8fbbe3501be4082f033c5cae49", "parents": ["1ec3e91e8f68f23e9a2a552426ca8da597e0ca8c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789413269, "git_changesets": ["8870e22c00ca9facfa41bea479f4090d840837ad"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28496": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jonathan Moss \u003cjmoss@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070972 - Repeat the loopback video test frame with imagefreeze  a=pascalc\n\nUse the current v4l2loopback control IDs. Repeat one green frame with GStreamer imagefreeze so the producer continues to supply frames while tests open and close the video device. The existing cleanup stops the producer.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325488\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325820\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/runtests.py"], "git_node": "fc1b69b94d0b9dc27bc396c4b905a6d9773b30ef", "git_parents": ["8870e22c00ca9facfa41bea479f4090d840837ad"], "node": "b05e1d696df9f28a468cb4bfc7fa8d231a598280", "parents": ["b5a060dfc4a2cb8fbbe3501be4082f033c5cae49"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789413336, "git_changesets": ["fc1b69b94d0b9dc27bc396c4b905a6d9773b30ef"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28497": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062740  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318094\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325804\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientOpenWindowUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "71fc2598dc424626c9090513dbf3b0a680108298", "git_parents": ["fc1b69b94d0b9dc27bc396c4b905a6d9773b30ef"], "node": "7452fd1d70a339895a2fd13c692c1d09f7eba71b", "parents": ["b05e1d696df9f28a468cb4bfc7fa8d231a598280"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062740 - Test.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322564\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325805\n", "files": ["dom/notification/test/mochitest/openWindow.serviceworker.js"], "git_node": "d2d462a44e4e691a137b69554e621a2927954492", "git_parents": ["71fc2598dc424626c9090513dbf3b0a680108298"], "node": "43fcbaa271d25e12d6a67008b65e90754838d958", "parents": ["7452fd1d70a339895a2fd13c692c1d09f7eba71b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789413526, "git_changesets": ["71fc2598dc424626c9090513dbf3b0a680108298", "d2d462a44e4e691a137b69554e621a2927954492"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28498": {"changesets": [{"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070028 - Fix confirm/alert dialogs not shown when triggered from a webextensions popup and sidebar panels.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324922\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325793\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-action.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_browserAction_popup_confirm_dialog.js", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "9450e744eed4935b379d5d43750f1b482e0487e6", "git_parents": ["d2d462a44e4e691a137b69554e621a2927954492"], "node": "c6d98ece55f98426eccf2e2b15be94adb0192081", "parents": ["43fcbaa271d25e12d6a67008b65e90754838d958"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789413564, "git_changesets": ["9450e744eed4935b379d5d43750f1b482e0487e6"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28499": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070871 - Reuse the pending MLS fallback when PortalLocationProvider::Watch is called again.  a=pascalc\n\nWatch() runs for every new geolocation request while the provider stays\nstarted. While the portal has not delivered a position yet, each call\nreplaced the MLSFallback without shutting the previous one down, so its\nNetworkGeolocationProvider stayed alive with its repeating timer and wifi\nlistener for the rest of the session.\n\nReuse the existing fallback instead, and add a gtest that counts the armed\nfallback timers across repeated Watch() calls.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324916\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325761\n", "files": ["dom/system/linux/PortalLocationProvider.cpp", "dom/system/linux/gtest/TestPortalLocationProvider.cpp", "dom/system/linux/gtest/moz.build", "dom/system/linux/moz.build"], "git_node": "90522773ea951542f452680b7c55c412178dfc1e", "git_parents": ["9450e744eed4935b379d5d43750f1b482e0487e6"], "node": "c30362a2edc12f46510f762f3a91175c48e83c05", "parents": ["c6d98ece55f98426eccf2e2b15be94adb0192081"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789414160, "git_changesets": ["90522773ea951542f452680b7c55c412178dfc1e"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28500": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070753 - Put the host's tokens first in the search CTA's derived query -  a=pascalc\n\nThe `dnsNotFound` Search CTA built its query as the path's keywords followed by the host's, so the site the user was trying to reach trailed the query. We want to lead with the host's tokens instead.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324814\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325760\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutNetError_searchCTA_derivation.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/netError.ftl", "toolkit/modules/URLKeywordAnalyzer.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/tests/xpcshell/test_URLKeywordAnalyzer.js"], "git_node": "64900e0208b305c5f9bb16a5fa7af39986438daf", "git_parents": ["90522773ea951542f452680b7c55c412178dfc1e"], "node": "d5fd9477257d46f091311c9c4907229b8cf94e30", "parents": ["c30362a2edc12f46510f762f3a91175c48e83c05"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789414190, "git_changesets": ["64900e0208b305c5f9bb16a5fa7af39986438daf"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28501": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070622 - Report which network geolocation service each request used  a=pascalc\n\nRecord telemetry for the host of geo.provider.network.url as GLS, BeaconDB or\nsomething else, and record that category in the geolocation.network_provider\nlabeled counter for every request the NetworkGeolocationProvider sends.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325201\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325728\n", "files": ["dom/geolocation/metrics.yaml", "dom/geolocation/test/unit/test_geolocation_provider.js", "dom/geolocation/test/unit/test_geolocation_provider_url.js", "dom/geolocation/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "dom/system/NetworkGeolocationProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e33dfe23a5761444b9f005375c28d4378d07c68d", "git_parents": ["64900e0208b305c5f9bb16a5fa7af39986438daf"], "node": "767054efc60dc9c40e3e3eaa7d0d2bc1356e9c55", "parents": ["d5fd9477257d46f091311c9c4907229b8cf94e30"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789414230, "git_changesets": ["e33dfe23a5761444b9f005375c28d4378d07c68d"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28502": {"changesets": [{"author": "Ted Campbell \u003ctcampbell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071475: Disable secondary sentry data sources in Fenix.  a=pascalc\n\nSentry has a complex set of options and their defaults often change so begin to\nlock down our expectations and assert them. Functionally this patch also disables\nhealth pings, ANRs and caught-exception handling. We can revisit re-enabling them\nin the future when we have been tie in to Fenix settings and more test coverage.\nThese changes are also applied to Focus via the shared lib-crash code.\n\nThis also removes the Sentry performance monitor ContentProvider from startup since\nthe feature was already disabled for us.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325521\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325737\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/crash-sentry/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/crash-sentry/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/crash/sentry/SentryService.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/crash-sentry/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/crash/sentry/SentryFeatureGatesTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/crash-sentry/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/crash/sentry/SentryServiceTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Analytics.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/Components.kt"], "git_node": "df3734a1b46b243828806b7001eb754d38edc8ed", "git_parents": ["e33dfe23a5761444b9f005375c28d4378d07c68d"], "node": "48536d83c0b56a39aeeba6d7a8975357a4ecfb2a", "parents": ["767054efc60dc9c40e3e3eaa7d0d2bc1356e9c55"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789419106, "git_changesets": ["df3734a1b46b243828806b7001eb754d38edc8ed"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28503": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from main\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-en-rCA/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-en-rCA/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-es-rES/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-en-rCA/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cs/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-el/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-en-rCA/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rES/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-iw/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nb-rNO/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml"], "git_node": "b13a3d9a7f5e03fe43a30d25cd92093c