 1789575924, "git_changesets": ["762a9d78a2cbd772fe6c80c19755a06fe50b6c79"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28520": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 27e472ab3c74195252a3547c00ad6a8d298cf629 with FIREFOX_157_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "6dec4318529f004fc94596bad5d1a7aee05ab34c", "git_parents": ["762a9d78a2cbd772fe6c80c19755a06fe50b6c79"], "node": "d1ffaf99cca071f77d8c9d9f9ec32698d5bc4e1a", "parents": ["b54c461753262f7da41843679e6cde86751196f0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789576427, "git_changesets": ["6dec4318529f004fc94596bad5d1a7aee05ab34c"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28521": {"changesets": [{"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071704 - Use a currentColor color-mix for the ghost button hover and active backgrounds in the native theme.  a=pascalc\n\nThe toolbar button tokens map back to ghost, restoring the reference bug 2069042 removed; every regime resolves to the value it did before.\n\nGhost's forced-colors values become explicit: the pinned native-theme value shadows the ones it inherited through --button-background-color-hover and -active.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325786\n\n(cherry picked from commit 35fbc58d44b7a114d216a3ddfec63843853c33d1)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325975\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_tokens.scss", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbarbutton.tokens.json"], "git_node": "b4c10153f0ec32273143f104ac62d847c519bd98", "git_parents": ["31f69ef6ea202c4908e502d0813d70c94b464b5c"], "node": "fb02826ad6fe91d324ab7819ec7380ac375fd22c", "parents": ["2fba56bce73021c24355ebe0882f5254161794ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071707 - Give the ghost button's resting text color a high contrast value in chrome.  a=pascalc\n\nOnly chrome changes: in-content already resolved both values through the brand layer.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325787\n\n(cherry picked from commit 7c5557a7170097c3c9dcc59bfd071aed69dd6724)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325973\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-brand.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/button.tokens.json"], "git_node": "7d5f77359e6343f64731c4a730ecfe5e553a8c3d", "git_parents": ["b4c10153f0ec32273143f104ac62d847c519bd98"], "node": "a4a205b2ccfc0d4a40a16d392d0613d4110d0515", "parents": ["fb02826ad6fe91d324ab7819ec7380ac375fd22c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789578990, "git_changesets": ["b4c10153f0ec32273143f104ac62d847c519bd98", "7d5f77359e6343f64731c4a730ecfe5e553a8c3d"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28522": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071678 - Flip active / inactive frame color in private window theme.  a=pascalc\n\nThis gets the color that Figma shows on the active window. I _think_\nthis is because Figma has some sort of rgba(0, 0, 0, .1) drop shadow\nwhich effectively makes it a bit darker?\n\nBut not an expert on our Figma stuff so please double-check.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325685\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326125\n", "files": ["browser/themes/addons/privatewindow/manifest.in.json"], "git_node": "264c5b47da393b6ba38fc7a8cf4179ea09e57e75", "git_parents": ["7d5f77359e6343f64731c4a730ecfe5e553a8c3d"], "node": "1f6854a6a9968786836378731d1e73f09b0b3a66", "parents": ["a4a205b2ccfc0d4a40a16d392d0613d4110d0515"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579014, "git_changesets": ["264c5b47da393b6ba38fc7a8cf4179ea09e57e75"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28523": {"changesets": [{"author": "Jens Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071182 - Keep NetworkGeolocationProvider shut down when a request settles after shutdown().  a=pascalc\n\nThe backoff handling added in bug 2048118 calls resetTimer() from the\nrequest completion paths. Neither checks whether the provider is still\nstarted, so a request that was in flight when shutdown() ran re-armed the\nrepeating timer and the provider kept issuing requests with no listener for\nthe rest of the session. Every system-provider fallback start/cancel cycle\ncould leave one such instance behind.\n\nMake resetTimer() a no-op once the provider is shut down, and abort in-flight\nrequests from shutdown() so they settle right away. Add an xpcshell test that\nshuts the provider down mid-request and checks that no provider timer\nremains once the request completes.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325308\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326417\n", "files": ["dom/geolocation/test/unit/test_geolocation_provider_shutdown.js", "dom/geolocation/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "dom/system/NetworkGeolocationProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "cf4b8cfe3bc60f165486b91b4bc358b4446908ae", "git_parents": ["264c5b47da393b6ba38fc7a8cf4179ea09e57e75"], "node": "98ad1df793e71cde8aa35a119c34264bf99c8a66", "parents": ["1f6854a6a9968786836378731d1e73f09b0b3a66"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579078, "git_changesets": ["cf4b8cfe3bc60f165486b91b4bc358b4446908ae"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28524": {"changesets": [{"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071068 - Use SegmentedVector on the popup painting code.  a=pascalc\n\nTo prevent WeakFrame from being memmove()d. This is an upliftable\nlow-risk fix.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325322\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326433\n", "files": ["layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp"], "git_node": "105827ba662f035f9dace958c06af26580b054cf", "git_parents": ["cf4b8cfe3bc60f165486b91b4bc358b4446908ae"], "node": "d8ecbbeb7723a6edc43d8f3579b286c8c5762dd9", "parents": ["98ad1df793e71cde8aa35a119c34264bf99c8a66"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579158, "git_changesets": ["105827ba662f035f9dace958c06af26580b054cf"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28525": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071030 - Merge directions when an RTP header extension is registered again with a different direction.  a=pascalc\n\nRegistering the same extension URI with different directions used to create\ntwo extmap entries with different ids for the same URI. Merge the directions\ninto the existing entry instead, so that a URI always maps to a single id.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325876\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325980\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.cpp", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_session_unittest.cpp"], "git_node": "1ee3e966a86a0774257a12dee59924c5fc037684", "git_parents": ["105827ba662f035f9dace958c06af26580b054cf"], "node": "75f605f4a89953f3c188dbb6b846ae74cc581ef6", "parents": ["d8ecbbeb7723a6edc43d8f3579b286c8c5762dd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andreas Pehrson \u003capehrson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071030 - Negotiate the dependency descriptor RTP header extension for receiving video.  a=pascalc\n\nlibwebrtc 152 rejects temporal units whose spatial indices are not strictly\nincreasing. Without the dependency descriptor, AV1 frames are handled by the\nsequence-number-only reference finder which stamps every frame with spatial\nindex 0, so layered AV1 streams (e.g. L2T3_KEY) never decode. Always offer the\ndependency descriptor for receiving video, and keep sending it for simulcast.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325877\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325981\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_basicAudioVideoVerifyExtmap.html", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_basicAudioVideoVerifyExtmapSendonly.html", "media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/jsep_session_unittest.cpp"], "git_node": "4bad8a9259b3447fc55bdea154fa9d27f3cdd323", "git_parents": ["1ee3e966a86a0774257a12dee59924c5fc037684"], "node": "ea9d050f439d1141dbd8fc5e4832c5b102144a9b", "parents": ["75f605f4a89953f3c188dbb6b846ae74cc581ef6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579274, "git_changesets": ["1ee3e966a86a0774257a12dee59924c5fc037684", "4bad8a9259b3447fc55bdea154fa9d27f3cdd323"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28526": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070836 - Fix snap-upstream-build tasks by ensuring newtab-node-modules is part of the toolchain.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325908\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326195\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/snap-upstream-build/kind.yml"], "git_node": "3998d58e1299ae668955d5e96996a0fbfac8b77b", "git_parents": ["4bad8a9259b3447fc55bdea154fa9d27f3cdd323"], "node": "226b03879a50d218810dfe5d8757db950c76fe9d", "parents": ["ea9d050f439d1141dbd8fc5e4832c5b102144a9b"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579316, "git_changesets": ["3998d58e1299ae668955d5e96996a0fbfac8b77b"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28527": {"changesets": [{"author": "Martin Stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070815 [Wayland] Disable session restore on Gnome due to Bug 2064100  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324876\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326135\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp"], "git_node": "53584648ff447f9163bc59c67e6bb21aedf0363f", "git_parents": ["3998d58e1299ae668955d5e96996a0fbfac8b77b"], "node": "6b08b5bc548f7940bbd9a45282f8b2969701ee18", "parents": ["226b03879a50d218810dfe5d8757db950c76fe9d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579378, "git_changesets": ["53584648ff447f9163bc59c67e6bb21aedf0363f"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28528": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069804 - Backport an upstream libvpx VP8 fix  a=pascalc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326359\n", "files": ["media/libvpx/libvpx/vp8/common/reconinter.c", "media/libvpx/moz.yaml", "media/libvpx/vp8_clamp_fullpixel_chroma_mv.patch"], "git_node": "a98bbd4291b71d46fe20247c5a675ce2bde2afda", "git_parents": ["53584648ff447f9163bc59c67e6bb21aedf0363f"], "node": "cb35da7b638fc8cb30fac0865db5f0142d6f3dc9", "parents": ["6b08b5bc548f7940bbd9a45282f8b2969701ee18"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579515, "git_changesets": ["a98bbd4291b71d46fe20247c5a675ce2bde2afda"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28529": {"changesets": [{"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069604 - Split --menuitem-padding into --menuitem-padding-block and --menuitem-padding-inline.  a=pascalc\n\nBehavior-neutral: every site that set the shorthand now sets the pair, and the shorthand is gone, so an override can no longer set padding that the block value doesn't see.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324633\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326046\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/global-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/menu.css"], "git_node": "0f62587dd356f98e530e7edc8840b34953a708e6", "git_parents": ["a98bbd4291b71d46fe20247c5a675ce2bde2afda"], "node": "207f555bf3a1684e521540fb4c27eb1af80c760d", "parents": ["cb35da7b638fc8cb30fac0865db5f0142d6f3dc9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069604 - Drop the always-zero --panel-menuitem-margin-block.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324634\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326047\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/panel-menuitem.tokens.json"], "git_node": "be54f125b8763c284ef522e0a4a239b60ed684df", "git_parents": ["0f62587dd356f98e530e7edc8840b34953a708e6"], "node": "d497949d07fc73dd43044ff3819c15cb69cc8647", "parents": ["207f555bf3a1684e521540fb4c27eb1af80c760d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069604 - Scroll a menupopup by whole menuitems.  a=pascalc\n\nRouting the padding and margins through variables computes to the values they had, except that the Windows menu icon's block margin is now split evenly across both sides so that a single variable can carry it, which leaves the item height alone and centers the icon in the line box.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324636\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326048\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/chrome.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_menupopup_scroll_amount.xhtml", "toolkit/themes/shared/menu.css", "toolkit/themes/windows/global/global.css"], "git_node": "c76341aba976af825225b8d5224ba2b0b1765fd0", "git_parents": ["be54f125b8763c284ef522e0a4a239b60ed684df"], "node": "1c002a7990677f8e986c7bd2150ad1f6c3b30642", "parents": ["d497949d07fc73dd43044ff3819c15cb69cc8647"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579589, "git_changesets": ["0f62587dd356f98e530e7edc8840b34953a708e6", "be54f125b8763c284ef522e0a4a239b60ed684df", "c76341aba976af825225b8d5224ba2b0b1765fd0"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28530": {"changesets": [{"author": "Meg Viar \u003clmegviar@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068992 - Add priority and scope auto-triggering set default and pin to startup on the first profile  a=pascalc\n\nThis patch ensures that the auto-triggering of set default and pin for users who will see an OS-level consent prompt only occur on first startup on the first profile and do not trigger for new selectable profiles. It also addresses the inconsistent behavior noted in the STR of the bug by adding a priority so that it takes precedence over [[ https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/source/browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs#2345 | FXA_ACCOUNTS_BADGE_REVISED ]].\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324750\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326489\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d5fadda1c5ea00906fe248ec66d2d716a7929b2b", "git_parents": ["c76341aba976af825225b8d5224ba2b0b1765fd0"], "node": "e274ef80a88f5fd24acafb38d223adb1dcba0e8f", "parents": ["1c002a7990677f8e986c7bd2150ad1f6c3b30642"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579628, "git_changesets": ["d5fadda1c5ea00906fe248ec66d2d716a7929b2b"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28531": {"changesets": [{"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068580 - Vendor the Metal backend at the pinned llama.cpp revision.  a=pascalc\n\nThe Metal files were taken from an older llama.cpp than the revision moz.yaml\npins, which is why they had to be in \"keep\" rather than revendored.\n\nThis vendors the backend at 74ade527 instead, matching llama.cpp. At that rev,\nit is split into a few files. The embedding of the shader source is unchanged: the\n.metal file still has the __embed_ggml-common.h__ and ggml-metal-impl.h\nplaceholders generate_metal_embed.py substitutes. etc.\n\nggml-metal-device.m and ggml-metal-device.cpp would compile to the same object\nname, so run_parser.py renames the former to ggml-metal-device-m.m, like it\nalready does for ggml.c and ggml-cpu.c.\n\nTwo patches are needed on top: \u003cmemory\u003e for std::unique_ptr in ggml-metal.cpp,\nand a guard around -[MTLSharedEvent waitUntilSignaledValue:timeoutMS:], which\nis macOS 12 while we deploy to 10.15 (11.0 on aarch64).\n\n`mach vendor --patch-mode check` now reproduces the tree.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322929\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326524\n", "files": ["third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-common.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-context.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-context.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device-m.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-impl.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal", "third_party/llama.cpp/metal-event-availability.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/missing-includes.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.build", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml", "third_party/llama.cpp/run_parser.py"], "git_node": "df26fa6415390d3491a670eeed39bde34a81469f", "git_parents": ["d5fadda1c5ea00906fe248ec66d2d716a7929b2b"], "node": "ac7d86053651ead2731fbf514884c0bb0ed9f2bf", "parents": ["e274ef80a88f5fd24acafb38d223adb1dcba0e8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068580 - Fall back to the general mat-vec kernel when Metal lacks the _short one.  a=pascalc\n\nggml_metal_library_get_pipeline_mul_mv asks for a _short kernel variant when\nne00 \u003c 32. On the macOS 15 machines the Metal compiler does not emit those\nspecializations from the vendored shader source, so the lookup fails with\n\n  MTLLibraryErrorDomain Code=5 \"Function kernel_mul_mv_f32_f32_short was not\n  found in the library\"\n\nget_pipeline_mul_mv returns a null pipeline and the caller encodes it without\nchecking.\n\nllama.cpp doesn't use this path, parakeet.cpp does, we can simply use the general\nkernel, which lives in the same source, it is emitted everywhere, and handles any size.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324025\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326525\n", "files": ["third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device-m.m", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/metal-mul-mv-short-fallback.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "89ea591fb34ecd0774e1ec449b5285b29fc33efe", "git_parents": ["df26fa6415390d3491a670eeed39bde34a81469f"], "node": "f073a074d385bbc72f3bb49dce1efeb9e2534130", "parents": ["ac7d86053651ead2731fbf514884c0bb0ed9f2bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068580 - Reassemble the embedded Metal shader when it changes.  a=pascalc\n\nEditing ggml-metal.metal did not change the built binary, very confusing.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324026\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326526\n", "files": ["third_party/llama.cpp/generate_metal_embed.py"], "git_node": "d3f2a562d7f7cac391429f947e26e9f2d2dbd708", "git_parents": ["89ea591fb34ecd0774e1ec449b5285b29fc33efe"], "node": "9bee1fb0427a5b314643e8d337c83b4056ee5e47", "parents": ["f073a074d385bbc72f3bb49dce1efeb9e2534130"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068758 - Don't attempt to use Metal in the Inference content process.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324021\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326527\n", "files": ["config/external/mozinference/mozinference.symbols", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/include/ggml-metal.h", "third_party/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.cpp", "third_party/llama.cpp/metal-disable.patch", "third_party/llama.cpp/moz.yaml", "toolkit/components/ml/backends/llama/LlamaRuntimeLinker.cpp", "toolkit/components/ml/backends/llama/LlamaRuntimeLinker.h"], "git_node": "a922bd6877a30a4d4c410beea48afc37a85c4279", "git_parents": ["d3f2a562d7f7cac391429f947e26e9f2d2dbd708"], "node": "a6712341cc03c4658e943dbe0a628087e6218f24", "parents": ["9bee1fb0427a5b314643e8d337c83b4056ee5e47"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789579788, "git_changesets": ["df26fa6415390d3491a670eeed39bde34a81469f", "89ea591fb34ecd0774e1ec449b5285b29fc33efe", "d3f2a562d7f7cac391429f947e26e9f2d2dbd708", "a922bd6877a30a4d4c410beea48afc37a85c4279"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28532": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from main\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-hi-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-oc/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-bqi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cs/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hy-rAM/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ia/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-iw/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-oc/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ro/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml"], "git_node": "8e6900838f425511d46c916b26d43aec1f2bc267", "git_parents": ["a922bd6877a30a4d4c410beea48afc37a85c4279"], "node": "4b31cfd197f4f6ae911716dbf54e3d984fa68cfa", "parents": ["a6712341cc03c4658e943dbe0a628087e6218f24"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789611350, "git_changesets": ["8e6900838f425511d46c916b26d43aec1f2bc267"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "28533": {"changesets": [{"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071067  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325229\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326795\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/composite/TextureHost.cpp"], "git_node": "6f89da6cca1c519f3f2f256c943bec6d8b161116", "git_parents": ["8e6900838f425511d46c916b26d43aec1f2bc267"], "node": "c7c1ce3690df3543cdd87dbcea1a6ca1a2785894", "parents": ["4b31cfd197f4f6ae911716dbf54e3d984fa68cfa"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789628736, "git_changesets": ["6f89da6cca1c519f3f2f256c943bec6d8b161116"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28534": {"changesets": [{"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068434.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324819\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326379\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/swgl/src/rasterize.h"], "git_node": "d6a4275acba801b20e27d06f8116bcd5bfecf939", "git_parents": ["6f89da6cca1c519f3f2f256c943bec6d8b161116"], "node": "aa7209446c2dbdd6ea5efd62c42f97219885beb0", "parents": ["c7c1ce3690df3543cdd87dbcea1a6ca1a2785894"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629143, "git_changesets": ["d6a4275acba801b20e27d06f8116bcd5bfecf939"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28535": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068422 - Fix fullscreen subdocument handling;  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325085\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326413\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h"], "git_node": "b43fe31b9c516a99aa03992a529d25804b5cad78", "git_parents": ["d6a4275acba801b20e27d06f8116bcd5bfecf939"], "node": "cf68e307d010099bfd65da008125a14b066876c9", "parents": ["aa7209446c2dbdd6ea5efd62c42f97219885beb0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629195, "git_changesets": ["b43fe31b9c516a99aa03992a529d25804b5cad78"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28536": {"changesets": [{"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068346 - Unwrap a copy in GetJSValFromKeyPathString.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326021\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326474\n", "files": ["dom/indexedDB/KeyPath.cpp"], "git_node": "56712bf34191011ccf75ccf696440301e0ebf37a", "git_parents": ["b43fe31b9c516a99aa03992a529d25804b5cad78"], "node": "a203767ab4f4642cb2a32d922e51fa9fb1f2d62d", "parents": ["cf68e307d010099bfd65da008125a14b066876c9"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629408, "git_changesets": ["56712bf34191011ccf75ccf696440301e0ebf37a"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28537": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061526 - Harden JAR URI deserialization  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D323545\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325865\n", "files": ["modules/libjar/nsJARURI.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/res/SubstitutingJARURI.h", "netwerk/protocol/res/SubstitutingProtocolHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "6b484f761d3ef9baa2d2fd27c4f7efef6dc501c2", "git_parents": ["56712bf34191011ccf75ccf696440301e0ebf37a"], "node": "a1422241719c1856c0917a54d8152a8de7dc6215", "parents": ["a203767ab4f4642cb2a32d922e51fa9fb1f2d62d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629583, "git_changesets": ["6b484f761d3ef9baa2d2fd27c4f7efef6dc501c2"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28538": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tomislav Jovanovic \u003ctomica@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057988 - Reject a duplicate conduit id.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325089\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326713\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/ConduitsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_subframes_privileges.html"], "git_node": "c02510998295acfd263721465201255c2db87322", "git_parents": ["6b484f761d3ef9baa2d2fd27c4f7efef6dc501c2"], "node": "a626fe04f7726ede809ef61402f8e8ebdbe2874e", "parents": ["a1422241719c1856c0917a54d8152a8de7dc6215"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629745, "git_changesets": ["c02510998295acfd263721465201255c2db87322"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28539": {"changesets": [{"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 1 - Rename ModulePaths to ModuleIdentifiers  a=pascalc\n\nRename-only, since ModuleIdentifiers will be used in later parts, instead of\njust paths.  No substantive changes.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324702\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325936\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.h", "dom/media/gmp/PGMP.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/PRDD.ipdl", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/RDDChild.h", "ipc/glue/PUtilityProcess.ipdl", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.cpp", "ipc/glue/UtilityProcessParent.h", "netwerk/ipc/PSocketProcess.ipdl", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/SocketProcessParent.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.h"], "git_node": "a8f9c2f02269c4b09241cb9e62c3f56e2c739f99", "git_parents": ["c02510998295acfd263721465201255c2db87322"], "node": "87702ea6e68d81579f45f429588f46021327c851", "parents": ["a626fe04f7726ede809ef61402f8e8ebdbe2874e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 2 - Pass child process's module list by section handle  a=pascalc\n\nChild processes now report loaded DLLs to the parent by section HANDLE instead\nof by filename.  The DLL blocklist's NtMapViewOfSection hook already receives\nthe section a module is being mapped from, so it duplicates that section,\nread-only, onto the ModuleLoadInfo for the load.  The parent identifies the\nmodule from the HANDLE.\n\nBecause the section outlives the view, this also fixes reporting for two kinds\nof load: a module the blocklist rejected, which is unmapped immediately, and a\nmodule unloaded before the parent processed the batch.  Previously, either\ncould be deleted before the parent had a chance to consider them.\n\nA handle cannot be forged into a reference to a different file and a child can\nonly send one it holds.  ValidateAndResolveModuleSection sanity checks:\n\n1. The section must map, and the view must be MEM_IMAGE. A data section can\n   be made over any openable file but an image section means the kernel\n   accepted the file as a PE and the child's image-load policy applied to it.\n2. The file must not be on a remote device.\n3. The file must not carry a mandatory integrity label below medium.\n\nThese checks replicate the checks of the MITIGATION_IMAGE_LOAD_NO_REMOTE and\nMITIGATION_IMAGE_LOAD_NO_LOW_LABEL child sandbox behaviors.  A child\ncan create a non-IMAGE section over any file it can open, so what it hands us\nis not bounded by the image-load policy.  The check avoid considering such\nfiles at all.  This currently applies to all child processes: content, gpu,\nRDD, socket, utility (all kinds), and GMP.  All have these sandbox mitigations.\n\nAlso fixes a couple of ways that a version resource could misuse VerQueryValueW's\noutput in the parent: a zero length underflowing to SIZE_MAX in\nQueryStringValue and a too-short buffer dereference in GetFromImage.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324703\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325937\n", "files": ["browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/DllBlocklist.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/ModuleLoadFrame.cpp", "browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/ModuleLoadFrame.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/media/gmp/GMPPlatform.h", "mozglue/misc/NativeNt.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/ModuleVersionInfo.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/WinDllServices.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/mozglue/ModuleLoadInfo.h"], "git_node": "aba7abec1b3de4246c030399cfb7e2e4ee2646ff", "git_parents": ["a8f9c2f02269c4b09241cb9e62c3f56e2c739f99"], "node": "1491990c8940c80ec1af37e1899f82645d2de320", "parents": ["87702ea6e68d81579f45f429588f46021327c851"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 3 - Test that UntrustedModulesProcessor rejects invalid modules  a=pascalc\n\nCheck that ValidateAndResolveModuleSection rejects descriptors that are\nnon-IMAGE sections or are for below-medium-integrity modules.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324704\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325938\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestModuleFileValidation.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "6966e484b6e8698d3b07a640c7280a78a984adbd", "git_parents": ["aba7abec1b3de4246c030399cfb7e2e4ee2646ff"], "node": "23f12c59c1ba34e0456e43ca1dd4086761a3eca8", "parents": ["1491990c8940c80ec1af37e1899f82645d2de320"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Parks \u003cdaparks@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057112: Part 4 - Add DLL-reporting failures to the third-party-modules ping  a=pascalc\n\nNow that the parent identifies a child process's modules from the section\nhandle the child sends, and silently skips any handle it cannot identify,\nwe will need telemetry for how often that skipping happens. This patch\nadds counters for that.\n\nunverifiableLoads: the number of module loads in child processes where the DLL\nblocklist hook reached the load but failed to duplicate the section handle.\n\nrejectedSections: the number of module section handles a child process sent\nto the parent that it refused as invalid module section handles.\n\nThe counters are per-process and are only ever incremented for child\nprocesses, so the browser process reports zero for both. The counters are\nreported by the process using the module, so their accuracy depends on\ntrusting the process itself. This is how the UntrustedModulesProcessor\nhas always worked, and is by design (for performance reasons).\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325939\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/docs/obsolete/collection/third-party-modules-ping.md", "toolkit/components/telemetry/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/other/UntrustedModules.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/other/UntrustedModulesDataSerializer.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesProcessor.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestModuleFileValidation.cpp", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/tests/gtest/TestUntrustedModules.cpp"], "git_node": "2c8bee635a0aec5b516ed8f877d731325a3f5a10", "git_parents": ["6966e484b6e8698d3b07a640c7280a78a984adbd"], "node": "14f44ca91d0c5ed75bbdb2f2e3b93547105dc1d4", "parents": ["23f12c59c1ba34e0456e43ca1dd4086761a3eca8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629874, "git_changesets": ["a8f9c2f02269c4b09241cb9e62c3f56e2c739f99", "aba7abec1b3de4246c030399cfb7e2e4ee2646ff", "6966e484b6e8698d3b07a640c7280a78a984adbd", "2c8bee635a0aec5b516ed8f877d731325a3f5a10"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28540": {"changesets": [{"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049352 - Clear mCallback before invoking Done() in the file, color, and application pickers.  a=pascalc\n\nSeveral picker and chooser handlers invoke mCallback and null the member\nafterwards. Move the callback into a local before invoking it, and return\nearly when it is already null, so each handler runs at most once.\n\nHandlers updated:\n  * widget/nsFilePickerProxy.cpp (Recv__delete__, ActorDestroy)\n  * widget/gtk/nsFilePicker.cpp (DoneNonPortal, DonePortal, DoneCommon)\n  * widget/gtk/nsColorPicker.cpp (Done)\n  * widget/gtk/nsApplicationChooser.cpp (Done)\n  * widget/cocoa/nsColorPicker.mm (Done)\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309753\n\n(cherry picked from commit 9218e63542cccf76054284d84f95c07f1b0b4332)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326717\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsColorPicker.mm", "widget/gtk/nsApplicationChooser.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsColorPicker.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsFilePicker.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsFilePicker.h", "widget/nsFilePickerProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "9939481ed92795164759ffd76e27e5049ec0eaac", "git_parents": ["2c8bee635a0aec5b516ed8f877d731325a3f5a10"], "node": "711d1e4796a8cd8c4d1be6cdf59e599126083cdb", "parents": ["14f44ca91d0c5ed75bbdb2f2e3b93547105dc1d4"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789629962, "git_changesets": ["9939481ed92795164759ffd76e27e5049ec0eaac"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28541": {"changesets": [{"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047721 - Clear VP9 frame-thread state on flush  a=pascalc\n\nCherry-pick of FFmpeg commit a024f8c5413d (avcodec/vp9: unref next_refs in\nvp9_decode_flush). vp9_decode_flush() releases s-\u003es.refs[] but not\ns-\u003enext_refs[], and vp9_decode_update_thread_context() seeds a worker's\nrefs[] from the source worker's next_refs[], so references from before a\nflush could survive it. Unref next_refs[] alongside refs[].\n\nThe commit is not in the FFmpeg 9.0 release branch, so it is carried as\nvp9-flush-unref-next-refs.patch and listed in README_MOZILLA to be\nre-applied on the next ffvpx update.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310961\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326597\n", "files": ["media/ffvpx/README_MOZILLA", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/vp9.c", "media/ffvpx/vp9-flush-unref-next-refs.patch"], "git_node": "9d1d9991a8b0287a2068c8efd6324c164a4e3976", "git_parents": ["9939481ed92795164759ffd76e27e5049ec0eaac"], "node": "6807d6cdd3369a626786a33b1b0c40d9429d0979", "parents": ["711d1e4796a8cd8c4d1be6cdf59e599126083cdb"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789630036, "git_changesets": ["9d1d9991a8b0287a2068c8efd6324c164a4e3976"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28542": {"changesets": [{"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041248 - Prevent NTLM login attempt with empty credentials  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326121\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326398\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpNTLMAuth.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpNTLMAuth.h"], "git_node": "160b0376ce8b00cb1f567424527282db0e41d824", "git_parents": ["9d1d9991a8b0287a2068c8efd6324c164a4e3976"], "node": "2e5159680b0c87faf82d6bcbf8533961fa13d52b", "parents": ["6807d6cdd3369a626786a33b1b0c40d9429d0979"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789630240, "git_changesets": ["160b0376ce8b00cb1f567424527282db0e41d824"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28543": {"changesets": [{"author": "Makoto Kato \u003cm_kato@ga2.so-net.ne.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028871 - Init should clear variables.  a=pasca