 Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326209\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327266\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInputBase.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_dragdropURL.js", "toolkit/components/places/BookmarkHTMLUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/places/PlacesUtils.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "64d87c6885a7cb058b3af320ae03d30a09248833", "git_parents": ["a42390393c93db40d386be2e6171514c381dc56f"], "node": "695c6f64d2081fef7d4079d017923f4b692321cf", "parents": ["97b68051bbe42ea2c99729f7214a7be7380f49b1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789752292, "git_changesets": ["64d87c6885a7cb058b3af320ae03d30a09248833"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28585": {"changesets": [{"author": "Teodor Tanasoaia \u003cttanasoaia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069744 - Don't assume instance creation succeeded on windows.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326509\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327312\n", "files": ["gfx/wgpu_bindings/src/server.rs"], "git_node": "83bea93d0265378b193cc9582c162e753e5e4144", "git_parents": ["64d87c6885a7cb058b3af320ae03d30a09248833"], "node": "224e330917b7bc3d5df591568828adf0f744a8c8", "parents": ["695c6f64d2081fef7d4079d017923f4b692321cf"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789752330, "git_changesets": ["83bea93d0265378b193cc9582c162e753e5e4144"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28586": {"changesets": [{"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067254 - Improve the source URL provenance information for clipboard copies.  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325348\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327326\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsCopySupport.cpp", "dom/base/nsCopySupport.h", "dom/events/Clipboard.cpp", "dom/events/DataTransfer.cpp", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_clipboard_source_url.js", "dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_clipboard_disallowed.html"], "git_node": "608aafb7b4da235a7d04cdc7e4713e584e8ec3d4", "git_parents": ["83bea93d0265378b193cc9582c162e753e5e4144"], "node": "b8a57547713b90489e9314a6a4de852ffb0557ec", "parents": ["224e330917b7bc3d5df591568828adf0f744a8c8"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789752369, "git_changesets": ["608aafb7b4da235a7d04cdc7e4713e584e8ec3d4"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28587": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070478 - Fix macOS exception handling for child processes that don't register their own exception handler.  a=pascalc\n\nWhen we receive an exception that is not meant for us, we claim we\nwant to ignore the exception. However, what we actually tell the\nkernel is that we handled the exception and it can resume the thread\nthat crashed. This causes a crash loop where the process gets\ncontinually resumed at the crashing point, generating a new\nexception and then getting resumed again. It never gets terminated\nby the kernel.\n\nFix that by telling the kernel we didn't handle the exception, so\nthat the exception continues to propagate and the process crashes.\n\nDiscovered while writing tests where the updater binary crashes as\na child of xpcshell. The updater binary does not register an\nexception handler. The tests were failing with a timeout.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D324566\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327356\n", "files": ["toolkit/crashreporter/breakpad-client/mac/handler/exception_handler.cc", "toolkit/crashreporter/test/gtest/TestMacExceptionHandler.cpp", "toolkit/crashreporter/test/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "02e0c5b1e922f987a95115af313a8faab4f073cc", "git_parents": ["608aafb7b4da235a7d04cdc7e4713e584e8ec3d4"], "node": "cfe4bba91214aad7beeffc53e3f9ce119e370e73", "parents": ["b8a57547713b90489e9314a6a4de852ffb0557ec"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789752668, "git_changesets": ["02e0c5b1e922f987a95115af313a8faab4f073cc"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28588": {"changesets": [{"author": "Caleb Chan \u003ccachan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070783 - Wait for Places async updates before querying the bookmark result in test_openURL_isAddressBarUrlNavigation_bookmark.  a=pascalc\n\nThe newly-inserted bookmark wasn't guaranteed to be indexed before the\nurlbar query ran, so the result was sometimes missing from the popup.\nUrlbarTestUtils.pickResultAndWaitForLoad then got targetIndex -1 and\nspun forever in its \"select the target row\" loop, causing the perma/\nintermittent timeouts in this bug and its duplicate, Bug 2070889,\nregressed by Bug 2067175.\n\nAlso wait for frecency recalculation and accept either a plain\nbookmark match or the autofilled heuristic result for the bookmark,\nsince which one the urlbar produces depends on how quickly frecency\nfor the new URL gets computed; requiring a specific non-autofill row\nreintroduced the same targetIndex -1 hang under mach test --verify.\n\nAdditionally close the app-menu popup left open by\nIPProtection.init()/.uninit() in test_ipprotection_ready and properly\nawait popuphidden after IPProtectionPanel.close() in\ntest_ipprotection_panel_closed, both of which otherwise leaked into\nlater tests in the same file and produced an unrelated\n\"unexpected popup\" failure.\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D325110\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327360\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_trigger_listeners.js", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "297ac2988fb281902744ce8f6d60a6733ed30df8", "git_parents": ["02e0c5b1e922f987a95115af313a8faab4f073cc"], "node": "cb8eada6cf11d232c90392cc6eff5986b319f4f0", "parents": ["cfe4bba91214aad7beeffc53e3f9ce119e370e73"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789752713, "git_changesets": ["297ac2988fb281902744ce8f6d60a6733ed30df8"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28589": {"changesets": [{"author": "Neeco Fabian \u003cneecofabian@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070459 - Fix focus outline overlap in FRO Terms of Use screen  a=pascalc\n\n- Add extra bottom margin, tweak bottom border radius of Manage data collection settings button\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326303\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327386\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "8a620d7ea41b5346f9eb094fdec7b583392d97a0", "git_parents": ["297ac2988fb281902744ce8f6d60a6733ed30df8"], "node": "6f30632f28fdb7a10e0eb7c61aad48dc732bec00", "parents": ["cb8eada6cf11d232c90392cc6eff5986b319f4f0"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789752868, "git_changesets": ["8a620d7ea41b5346f9eb094fdec7b583392d97a0"], "user": "pchevrel@mozilla.com"}, "28590": {"changesets": [{"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072433, don't leak elements with animated classes,  a=pascalc\n\nOriginal Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D326773\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327401\n", "files": ["dom/base/ContentList.cpp", "dom/base/ContentList.h", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.h"], "git_node": "23c3c05024c4665bedcc2680f5e1e649955ea4c2", "git_parents": ["8a620d7ea41b5346f9eb094fdec7b583392d97a0"], "node": "313ef670d5cc7b755e4f1290fd615e27f0c78503", "parents": ["6f30632f28fdb7a10e0eb7c61aad48dc732bec00"], "tags": []}], "date": 1789753063, "git_changesets": 